                {
                    "name": "places/ChIJvbGg56pZwokRp_E3JbivnLQ/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSURiMWNxazRnRRAB",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a week ago",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "Bryant Park is an urban oasis in the heart of NYC, perfect for a family visit. The library is on the other side.\nWe encountered a live jazz session on a weekday evening. When you walk into the park, you're greeted by lush greenery, towering trees, and vibrant flower beds. It's a welcome contrast to the bustling city streets surrounding it. The kids will love the open space to run around and play. There's a charming carousel they can ride on, which adds a touch of magic to the experience.\n\nFor a relaxing break, you can find plenty of seating, from classic park benches to cozy lawn chairs. The park also offers free Wi-Fi, so you can easily share your experiences with friends and family. In the summer, there are often outdoor movie nights, which can be a fun way to wind down the day with your kids.\n\nIf you're visiting in the winter, the park transforms into a winter wonderland with an ice skating rink and holiday shops. No matter the season, Bryant Park provides a tranquil yet lively environment where the whole family can unwind and enjoy the beauty of NYC. Plus, its central location makes it a convenient stop during your sightseeing adventures.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
