                {
                    "name": "places/ChIJvbGg56pZwokRp_E3JbivnLQ/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUR6X2FiNElREAE",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 months ago",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "Bryant Park is a fantastic urban oasis in the heart of Midtown Manhattan! We had such a wonderful time here with our family. The sprawling lawn is perfect for kids to run around and burn off energy, while parents can relax on the grass or at one of the many tables and chairs scattered throughout the park.\n\nWe loved grabbing lunch from the nearby food kiosks and enjoying it in the park. There are so many great options for food and coffee surrounding the area.\n\nThe park's central location is incredibly convenient, with the New York Public Library right next door and several subway stations just steps away.\n\nThe park offers a variety of free activities and amenities that kept our whole family entertained. We particularly enjoyed the putting green and the carousel, which were big hits with the kids.\n\nThe atmosphere is lively yet relaxing, with a mix of locals and tourists enjoying the beautiful green space amidst the city's skyscrapers. We're so grateful for this family-friendly spot in Manhattan and can't wait to return on our next visit to the city!",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
