                },
                {
                    "name": "places/ChIJd7I1IO5ZwokRbv7YUlgChl4/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSURMZ19ibGlBRRAB",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a month ago",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "The skyscraper with the best view in New York City, 360°, however it is not the most beautiful in terms of architecture (Empire State and The Rock are better to admire from the inside).\n\nAnother advantage is that it is interactive, what it lacks in interior design it makes up for with interactive rooms on 3 different floors and with many mirrors where you can take very original photos with the skyscrapers in the background.\n\nIt is important to consider that the entrance is from the bottom of the Central Station, not from the street outside, to avoid wasting time if you are already at the limit of the reserved time.\n\nThere is a bar and the classic souvenir shop, with high prices and more limited products than the Empire State store.\n\nIt is advisable to make a reservation in advance and arrive 15 or 10 minutes before the indicated time.\n\nBefore going up, they take you to watch a video in a small room, then a photo that you don't have to buy, and then they give you some foot protectors that you have to use.  With the bracelet they put at the entrance you can register a code before entering the elevator to one of the interactive rooms on the floors above.\n\nIn general it takes around 20 min.  go to the elevator.  Once up, you can stay for an unlimited time but you cannot go back from one floor to another.\n\nAt some point the mirrors can make you feel a little bit dizzy.\n\nA visit to the toilet is mandatory on the 3rd floor.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
                        "text": "The skyscraper with the best view in New York City, 360°, however it is not the most beautiful in terms of architecture (Empire State and The Rock are better to admire from the inside).\n\nAnother advantage is that it is interactive, what it lacks in interior design it makes up for with interactive rooms on 3 different floors and with many mirrors where you can take very original photos with the skyscrapers in the background.\n\nIt is important to consider that the entrance is from the bottom of the Central Station, not from the street outside, to avoid wasting time if you are already at the limit of the reserved time.\n\nThere is a bar and the classic souvenir shop, with high prices and more limited products than the Empire State store.\n\nIt is advisable to make a reservation in advance and arrive 15 or 10 minutes before the indicated time.\n\nBefore going up, they take you to watch a video in a small room, then a photo that you don't have to buy, and then they give you some foot protectors that you have to use.  With the bracelet they put at the entrance you can register a code before entering the elevator to one of the interactive rooms on the floors above.\n\nIn general it takes around 20 min.  go to the elevator.  Once up, you can stay for an unlimited time but you cannot go back from one floor to another.\n\nAt some point the mirrors can make you feel a little bit dizzy.\n\nA visit to the toilet is mandatory on the 3rd floor.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "authorAttribution": {
                        "displayName": "Patricia Islas",
                        "uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116177658611228438398/reviews",
                        "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVfZ9LkkIOvPFAsv-P25EtD9bIUZZPg3k8jg6Vk5XtmGbrmP-53=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4"
