                {
                    "name": "places/ChIJd7I1IO5ZwokRbv7YUlgChl4/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNyeXBuellREAE",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a month ago",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "What an amazing, immersive experience. I’ve been to the top of the Empire State Building. I’ve been to Top of the Rock.  They are great experiences, but nothing compares to SUMMIT One. It’s as much about the experience in the building as much as it is about the view.  Stellar views of Manhattan and the surrounding area are complimented by the highly mirrored, multi-level interior.l. Parts of the experience are about what’s on view, part is about what’s inside, and parts are equal interior and exterior.  If you buy your tickets in advance you’ll be asked to come no sooner than 5 minutes prior to start (but they’ll start lining up 15 minutes prior) and no later than 30 minutes after your time. Then you’ll receive an email recommending how much time you should spend in each area.  I see why.  You get in and get so take by the views, the mirrors, the silver, the glass… you get lost just enjoying yourself. Get ready to take tons of pictures.  Eventually you’ll make your way to the top where you can stop for a bite and a drink at the rooftop bar.  It’s a great experience!!",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
                        "text": "What an amazing, immersive experience. I’ve been to the top of the Empire State Building. I’ve been to Top of the Rock.  They are great experiences, but nothing compares to SUMMIT One. It’s as much about the experience in the building as much as it is about the view.  Stellar views of Manhattan and the surrounding area are complimented by the highly mirrored, multi-level interior.l. Parts of the experience are about what’s on view, part is about what’s inside, and parts are equal interior and exterior.  If you buy your tickets in advance you’ll be asked to come no sooner than 5 minutes prior to start (but they’ll start lining up 15 minutes prior) and no later than 30 minutes after your time. Then you’ll receive an email recommending how much time you should spend in each area.  I see why.  You get in and get so take by the views, the mirrors, the silver, the glass… you get lost just enjoying yourself. Get ready to take tons of pictures.  Eventually you’ll make your way to the top where you can stop for a bite and a drink at the rooftop bar.  It’s a great experience!!",
                        "languageCode": "en"
