                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a week ago",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "The MetLife Building, built in 1909, is the headquarters of MetLife Insurance Company of the United States. The building is 700 feet (213 meters) tall and has 50 floors. It was the tallest skyscraper in the world until it was replaced by the Woolworth Building in 1913. The building was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1972 and on the National Register of Historic Places in 1978.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
