                {
                    "name": "places/ChIJTZmnm1VYwokRpy2xcCtdR3g/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSURCellINXFRRRAB",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a year ago",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "I went on Friday Jan 6th for the Solemn service for \"Epiphany\". There was a wonderful Organ Recital played by Dr. Gail Archer prior to the beginning of the service. Such beautiful music.\nI was really moved by the service itself, the chanting and singing during the Solemn Mass felt so meaniful. Thank you Dr.David Hurd & choir! The sermon given by Brother Jim Woodrum, SSJE was thoughtful, comforting and helpfully resonated with these days & times.\nI certainly plan to attend another service\nat Saint Mary's in the near future.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
                        "text": "I went on Friday Jan 6th for the Solemn service for \"Epiphany\". There was a wonderful Organ Recital played by Dr. Gail Archer prior to the beginning of the service. Such beautiful music.\nI was really moved by the service itself, the chanting and singing during the Solemn Mass felt so meaniful. Thank you Dr.David Hurd & choir! The sermon given by Brother Jim Woodrum, SSJE was thoughtful, comforting and helpfully resonated with these days & times.\nI certainly plan to attend another service\nat Saint Mary's in the near future.",
