                    "name": "places/ChIJT6hnZatZwokRVH08uIBJfSs/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNSalA3TTBnRRAB",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a year ago",
                    "rating": 4,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "At the corner of 7th avenue and 39th Street you will find Giant Needle and Button designed by Claes Oldenburg. A statue of a garment worker toils in the shadow of the huge needle and button. This weathered-looking bronze statue is a work by Judith Weller. It depicts her father, one of a great many Jewish immigrants who moved to New York and wound up working in the garment district. Looming over the immigrant worker, the needle and button feel less whimsical and more menacingly oppressive.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
