            "primaryType": "indian_restaurant",
            "shortFormattedAddress": "1247 First St SE, Washington",
            "editorialSummary": {
                "text": "Customized bowls of deeply-flavored Indian fare in stylish surrounds, plus beer, wine & gin/tonics.",
                "languageCode": "en"
            },
            "reviews": [
                {
                    "name": "places/ChIJPUSE6da5t4kRaWoh3Xkvw1g/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNyNnA3c0NREAE",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a month ago",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "The food at RASA was phenomenal! We got the chicken tikka, spicy chili chicken, and tumeric ginger shrimp. All were excellent and tasted fresh with lots of flavor. As my wife recently acquired a late-onset peanut allergy, RASA's allergy accommodations were also a great plus. Fun spot and a cool vibe for solid smart casual indian food.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
                        "text": "The food at RASA was phenomenal! We got the chicken tikka, spicy chili chicken, and tumeric ginger shrimp. All were excellent and tasted fresh with lots of flavor. As my wife recently acquired a late-onset peanut allergy, RASA's allergy accommodations were also a great plus. Fun spot and a cool vibe for solid smart casual indian food.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "authorAttribution": {
                        "displayName": "Sam Buck",
                        "uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/102345090807512960586/reviews",
                        "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVwhFP87gGrQ0YyUW7lV_AXOM7vW9d-IAPG2p-2uqYGKLbmo_0-rQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5"
                    },
                    "publishTime": "2024-07-06T03:13:42Z"
                },
                {
                    "name": "places/ChIJPUSE6da5t4kRaWoh3Xkvw1g/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNEODVfUjhnRRAB",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 months ago",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "Unique concept of Indian food combined with Mexican bowl theme. Taste was awesome, portion was enough to feed one person easily. Ambience was also refreshing.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
                        "text": "Unique concept of Indian food combined with Mexican bowl theme. Taste was awesome, portion was enough to feed one person easily. Ambience was also refreshing.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "authorAttribution": {
                        "displayName": "Hrishikesh Walunj",
                        "uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101646003523354314439/reviews",
                        "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWchaF_Sxch5U8wtakknOCt7h-tI3NZmbSWA2yAlBTdpEd9374=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4"
                    },
                    "publishTime": "2024-04-01T13:37:00Z"
                },
                {
                    "name": "places/ChIJPUSE6da5t4kRaWoh3Xkvw1g/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNMcWNlODd3RRAB",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a week ago",
                    "rating": 4,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "UPDATE Aug 2024: Lately it’s been much better here! The bowls are consistently tasty and healthy, and I haven’t stayed inside for more than a couple minutes each time (pickup orders only), so I can’t comment on the current state of the indoor mosquitoes (not taking that risk again! 😁).\n\nFood was solid and I like the colorful decor, but I got absolutely eaten alive by mosquitoes 🦟 inside. I think a bit of airflow (fan or A/C) or keeping the windows closed would go a long way to providing a more enjoyable dining atmosphere.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
                        "text": "UPDATE Aug 2024: Lately it’s been much better here! The bowls are consistently tasty and healthy, and I haven’t stayed inside for more than a couple minutes each time (pickup orders only), so I can’t comment on the current state of the indoor mosquitoes (not taking that risk again! 😁).\n\nFood was solid and I like the colorful decor, but I got absolutely eaten alive by mosquitoes 🦟 inside. I think a bit of airflow (fan or A/C) or keeping the windows closed would go a long way to providing a more enjoyable dining atmosphere.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "authorAttribution": {
                        "displayName": "Andy Lutz",
                        "uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/101409071778318694686/reviews",
                        "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVaksbRJGbE6YDytKuLaIK_gOjo3aHIHfdG9cBHUMOyEUYkKmdDpA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6"
                    },
                    "publishTime": "2024-08-06T19:37:37Z"
                },
                {
                    "name": "places/ChIJPUSE6da5t4kRaWoh3Xkvw1g/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUR0cGN6a3R3RRAB",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "6 months ago",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "RASA is very similar to CAVA, except that RASA is more Indian than Mediterranean. The selection is large and has lots of dairy-free, vegetarian, and vegans options. The prices are about $12-15 per person, similar to CAVA and Chipotle in DC.\n\nThe woman running the line today showed excellent service and was courteous enough to offer suggestions and allow me to try different items, given my first visit. I highly recommend eating at this location. The decorum aesthetic is pleasurable too.\n\nBe warned. The spiciness of certain dishes definitely fit Indian levels of spiciness.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
                        "text": "RASA is very similar to CAVA, except that RASA is more Indian than Mediterranean. The selection is large and has lots of dairy-free, vegetarian, and vegans options. The prices are about $12-15 per person, similar to CAVA and Chipotle in DC.\n\nThe woman running the line today showed excellent service and was courteous enough to offer suggestions and allow me to try different items, given my first visit. I highly recommend eating at this location. The decorum aesthetic is pleasurable too.\n\nBe warned. The spiciness of certain dishes definitely fit Indian levels of spiciness.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "authorAttribution": {
                        "displayName": "Arthur McNamara",
                        "uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/117159587140804589987/reviews",
                        "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJ6u2aZCuK0a4R94m_RBb-4iESDiG7dmYSOuqECNbILqPZW=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo"
                    },
                    "publishTime": "2024-02-05T21:03:42Z"
                },
                {
                    "name": "places/ChIJPUSE6da5t4kRaWoh3Xkvw1g/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSURyb09tMkxREAE",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a month ago",
                    "rating": 4,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "Solid place for quick Indian. Not all is authentic but everything has been tasty. Service is always good and quick. Excellent gravies and proteins. Stay away from the samosas and naan if you’re a purist but the food is still great for a good price.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
                        "text": "Solid place for quick Indian. Not all is authentic but everything has been tasty. Service is always good and quick. Excellent gravies and proteins. Stay away from the samosas and naan if you’re a purist but the food is still great for a good price.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
