                        {
                            "name": "places/ChIJPUSE6da5t4kRaWoh3Xkvw1g/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNCbmYzUWZ3EAE",
                            "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a year ago",
                            "rating": 5,
                            "text": {
                                "text": "As the street gets darker in Navy yards DC when you walk away from Nats Stadium and you pass by the not so interesting (but sometimes reliable) Chipotle, you will find this amazing space called Rasa. The moment I entered Rasa I knew this was gonna be fun. From deep meaningful painting at the entrance to the really cool music inviting you, the ambience passed the vibe check.\nThe bowl in Rasa is a mix of various cultures of India. The gravy sauces, the protein, veggies and the base all delicious. Even the supergrains, which can be bland in other places, are flavorful.\nOrdered for Spicy beef which had taste of kerala in it, but that topped with peanut sesame and tomato garlic sauce and side of mind blowingly delicious veggies that reminds you of different types of cuisines in India, gave a brilliant flavor profile that knocked me off my feet (not that I am gonna marry the dish but could’ve if it was a real person)\nThe staff was nice and helpful to give chutneys on the side.\nDon’t miss the Lassi too. One of the best in Nova/DC area.\nOnly thing missing was naan to complete the whole meal, but the blissful burp after the meal is telling me to ignore this nitpick.",
                                "languageCode": "en"
                            },
                            "originalText": {
