                        {
                            "name": "places/ChIJ7aCfw2C3t4kRvb6eK8AmDGQ/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUN4blByRXF3RRAB",
                            "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a year ago",
                            "rating": 3,
                            "text": {
                                "text": "We went here to celebrate my husbands birthday. We ordered the Sushi - which was the best thing on their whole menu (but the sushi rice was very dry which makes the sushi fall apart pretty quickly but the taste was 10/10). We also liked the nigiri, calamari and the shrimp appetizer which were good. Apart from these we also ordered the gyoza, 1000 layer potato and Dan Dan noodles & eggplant entree dishes. The gyoza was lacking flavor and was very bland, 1000 layer potatoes the same thing. Dan Dan & the eggplant dish were extremely salty without much flavors. We also liked the dessert which was bubble waffle with taro ice cream.  The service is good and our server was friendly and considerate but the lack of taste in a lot of dishes or too much salt was very off putting. The ambiance is great but you can hardly hear the next person talking as it’s super loud. Prices are little bit on the higher side. Overall if I ever go back that will probably be for the sushi only.",
                                "languageCode": "en"
                            },
