                {
                    "name": "places/ChIJE3EX2pO3t4kRtfRlVwm6pYg/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNGcDh6ZldnEAE",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a month ago",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "Great little vegan spot. Small menu,  but the food is delicious & healthy. Employees are friendly, & the owner is very nice & always greets customers with a big smile.\n\nI've tried the PB no J açai bowl (sub for almond butter), waffle, quesadilla, plant burger, southwest salad. My favorites are the plant burger & PB no J açai bowl. Great place for a healthy breakfast or lunch when in city center.\n\nI recently tried the veggie pizza for dinner. The homemade sour dough crust was delicious. And I'm always amazed at the vegan cheese. It tastes just like normal cheese to me.\n\nThe beet faster juice is very refreshing on a hot summer day.\n\nI really appreciate the thoughtfulness put into the interior design & decor as well. Feels like you're inside a small, well appointed library. The restroom is very clean & also decorated cutely with colorful floor tiles.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
