                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago",
                    "rating": 4,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "Stopped by for lunch on a weekday.\n\nYou order at a big touch screen at the front of the restaurant. This is great if you know what you want. I’d recommend looking at menu before arriving.\n\nThis is a fully plant based menu with things clearly labeled gluten free.\n\nI got the buddah bowl with gluten free fried chicken. The bowl was a good size. The fried chicken had a nice crunch outside but the inside wasn’t as firm as I was expecting.\n\nThe bowl had good flavor overall but I would have preferred more sauce.\n\nDecent amount of seating inside. Fairly quick to get food out.\n\nI will definitely come back next time I’m in DC.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
