            "editorialSummary": {
                "text": "Elegant Federalist townhouse featuring raw-vegan dishes & organic wine pairings on Friday evenings.",
                "languageCode": "en"
            },
            "reviews": [
                {
                    "name": "places/ChIJaa4QEpW3t4kR48t4GS8Qvgg/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSURqeWE2QzV3RRAB",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "Delightful fully vegan tasting menu.  Fantastic atmosphere and food.  Also loved the optional alcohol-free drink pairings.  The only negative I can share is that the price point is significant, though the quality of the food and the location don't make that especially surprising.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
                        "text": "Delightful fully vegan tasting menu.  Fantastic atmosphere and food.  Also loved the optional alcohol-free drink pairings.  The only negative I can share is that the price point is significant, though the quality of the food and the location don't make that especially surprising.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "authorAttribution": {
                        "displayName": "Lake Kubilius",
                        "uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/109943570988192977469/reviews",
                        "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVqPAwYBDDEvU-_iQuvm28LQr74ewOUZjYO84UqKpo8pZj6P-CH=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5"
                    },
                    "publishTime": "2024-05-04T18:22:35Z"
                },
                {
                    "name": "places/ChIJaa4QEpW3t4kR48t4GS8Qvgg/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNkMVlhMlJREAE",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "6 months ago",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "Went to Elizabeth’s for the first time to celebrate my birthday. It was an amazing experience! The place is so nice and romantic, and service was excellent from start to end, including our waiter, Elizabeth herself, and the sommelier.\nWe ordered the caviar and it was delicious, definitely worth the add-on! The menu was well-constructed and all of the dishes were so good by themselves and as a whole. The potato dish was so flavorful and yet so comforting, the truffle pasta was delicious, and the main course was surprising. We didn’t go with the pairing as I often feel like it’s too much wine for me, but I was happy to see that they have a half pairing option.\n\nI’m always excited to see a vegan fine dining place that’s so good and with a good crowd there! I’d happily bring by non-vegetarian friends here and I’m sure they would love it!\n\nThe only downside worth mentioning is that although I was full by the end of the meal, my partner was still hungry (and we had ordered the caviar in addition to the prix fixe)",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
                        "text": "Went to Elizabeth’s for the first time to celebrate my birthday. It was an amazing experience! The place is so nice and romantic, and service was excellent from start to end, including our waiter, Elizabeth herself, and the sommelier.\nWe ordered the caviar and it was delicious, definitely worth the add-on! The menu was well-constructed and all of the dishes were so good by themselves and as a whole. The potato dish was so flavorful and yet so comforting, the truffle pasta was delicious, and the main course was surprising. We didn’t go with the pairing as I often feel like it’s too much wine for me, but I was happy to see that they have a half pairing option.\n\nI’m always excited to see a vegan fine dining place that’s so good and with a good crowd there! I’d happily bring by non-vegetarian friends here and I’m sure they would love it!\n\nThe only downside worth mentioning is that although I was full by the end of the meal, my partner was still hungry (and we had ordered the caviar in addition to the prix fixe)",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "authorAttribution": {
                        "displayName": "Ana Luiza D.",
                        "uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/102705625386603550779/reviews",
                        "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjVcYvRjDQEXjhAFEukrt4rYbizvB5bIjs0mTP2nDarigOPgBO_T=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4"
                    },
                    "publishTime": "2024-02-17T00:09:57Z"
                },
                {
                    "name": "places/ChIJaa4QEpW3t4kR48t4GS8Qvgg/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUN0LU16T2p3RRAB",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "6 months ago",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "Dined at Elizabeth's for my birthday dinner and it was an amazing experience! The staff is very friendly and knowledgeable about each dish. Each dish was appealing to all senses and was an experience on its own! My favorites were the garlic truffle pasta and the Passion fruit sorbet palate cleanser. It was also admirable to see the owner work alongside her staff. We found out from the bartender downstairs that their fixed tasting menu changes every few months and that is more of a reason to stop by more than once a year!",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
                        "text": "Dined at Elizabeth's for my birthday dinner and it was an amazing experience! The staff is very friendly and knowledgeable about each dish. Each dish was appealing to all senses and was an experience on its own! My favorites were the garlic truffle pasta and the Passion fruit sorbet palate cleanser. It was also admirable to see the owner work alongside her staff. We found out from the bartender downstairs that their fixed tasting menu changes every few months and that is more of a reason to stop by more than once a year!",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "authorAttribution": {
                        "displayName": "Suhey Ortega",
                        "uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/118134833113239236696/reviews",
                        "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXRDOJOTFhfLvQ7GHi67pi0WlPC0ORrMLLnoGyfcZDe_nCO6QBisg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5"
                    },
                    "publishTime": "2024-01-28T21:37:42Z"
                },
                {
                    "name": "places/ChIJaa4QEpW3t4kR48t4GS8Qvgg/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNEbklubkpREAE",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 months ago",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "Every dish clearly had so much thought and technique put into it. The early courses are are on the small \"tasting\" side and I def wish I could have more of them especially the \"smoked salmon\" one, but they later courses become more normal sized portions so that you're full by the end.\n\nWe also had the Cheese platter which was worth sharing among 4 at $40 but the only thing that really stood out was the fig jam. The cheeses are made in house we're told but they all were really mild flavored. I'd even recommend savoring them without the provided crackers/plantains, though the plantains do add some salt.\n\nIf you go just for the prix fixe menu it's probably going to run you $150 with tax/tip, given how much even fast food vegan is now, that's not far off from several burgers.\n\nIt was also nice to see Elizabeth working the floor to the point that she removed dirty dishes from our table and we weren't quite sure if that was her or not :)",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
