                    "name": "places/ChIJs7PZzcO3t4kRxQIgwG5AjtQ/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUN6MC1pY3ZRRRAB",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 months ago",
                    "rating": 3,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "We had a chance to taste food from this restaurant RASA in Washington DC and it was sadly underwhelming.\nThe Ambience is nice, hip and colorful. It also has both outdoor and indoor seating.\n\nBut it falls flat in terms of taste and flavor, I mean some folks would find the fusion food interesting but if you’re expecting typical Indian palate you’d be disappointed.\nFood quality and quantity are good. They also have many varieties of bowl and snack items. Service is satisfactory, no complains.\nLarge vegan and vegetarian selection is available.\nOverall an average experience.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
                        "text": "We had a chance to taste food from this restaurant RASA in Washington DC and it was sadly underwhelming.\nThe Ambience is nice, hip and colorful. It also has both outdoor and indoor seating.\n\nBut it falls flat in terms of taste and flavor, I mean some folks would find the fusion food interesting but if you’re expecting typical Indian palate you’d be disappointed.\nFood quality and quantity are good. They also have many varieties of bowl and snack items. Service is satisfactory, no complains.\nLarge vegan and vegetarian selection is available.\nOverall an average experience.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
