            "editorialSummary": {
                "text": "Upscale New American kitchen featuring locally sourced, seasonal dishes in modern surrounds.",
                "languageCode": "en"
            },
            "reviews": [
                {
                    "name": "places/ChIJt6jHBLy3t4kRI2hxAOiO8fw/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNUeF9uY2VnEAE",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "3 months ago",
                    "rating": 3,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "Definitely did not meet expectations. The food in particular was disappointing, but service was fine and the atmosphere was fine too.\n\nThe risotto fritters were a delicious starter, we loved the crispy exterior and molten risotto underneath, accented perfectly with the garlic creme fraiche.\n\nThe beet salad we had was a pretty boring and average salad, nothing notable.\n\nThe crispy Roman style artichokes were poor, very disappointing dish.\n\nMy entree was the tile fish, and while the fish itself was bland, the accompanying sauce was pretty flavorful.\n\nHaving been overall quite underwhelmed by the initial dishes, we passed on dessert.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
                        "text": "Definitely did not meet expectations. The food in particular was disappointing, but service was fine and the atmosphere was fine too.\n\nThe risotto fritters were a delicious starter, we loved the crispy exterior and molten risotto underneath, accented perfectly with the garlic creme fraiche.\n\nThe beet salad we had was a pretty boring and average salad, nothing notable.\n\nThe crispy Roman style artichokes were poor, very disappointing dish.\n\nMy entree was the tile fish, and while the fish itself was bland, the accompanying sauce was pretty flavorful.\n\nHaving been overall quite underwhelmed by the initial dishes, we passed on dessert.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "authorAttribution": {
                        "displayName": "Saminda Wijegunawardena",
                        "uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103911639702535575368/reviews",
                        "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUSXXkgtqr0GB455Mc3JOtHuOOV-7Jma18NRDQlY_UI1HPtn5ER=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6"
                    },
                    "publishTime": "2024-05-19T20:45:10Z"
                },
                {
                    "name": "places/ChIJt6jHBLy3t4kRI2hxAOiO8fw/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUQ5anZfd1RREAE",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "5 months ago",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "Everything we ate was amazing. My husband and I ate the vegan 5 course taster. They were able to accommodate my gluten free needs with ease and we enjoyed 4 hrs of pampering eating outside with exceptional service from waiter Georgi. Chef/owner Todd came and checked on us at the beginning and end of our experience which made it all the more memorable for our family of four. Only remembered to take a few photos and some half way through eating, but every work of art was plated beautifully.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
                        "text": "Everything we ate was amazing. My husband and I ate the vegan 5 course taster. They were able to accommodate my gluten free needs with ease and we enjoyed 4 hrs of pampering eating outside with exceptional service from waiter Georgi. Chef/owner Todd came and checked on us at the beginning and end of our experience which made it all the more memorable for our family of four. Only remembered to take a few photos and some half way through eating, but every work of art was plated beautifully.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "authorAttribution": {
                        "displayName": "Virginia McDowell",
                        "uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/109086728267599211711/reviews",
                        "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjXmYJ8i7e70axQUnh_ccqtS-ioJBSQso-aeYVP8zpMJ2D4sue7rGA=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo"
                    },
                    "publishTime": "2024-03-16T19:35:04Z"
                },
                {
                    "name": "places/ChIJt6jHBLy3t4kRI2hxAOiO8fw/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUREemE2MXZBRRAB",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "4 months ago",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "I had the pleasure of going to Equinox 2 years ago as a solo diner, and Didier took care of me. It was such an amazing experience back THEN, that when it was time to decide to hear my birthday dinner was going to be this year, I knew where to go.\n\nTo my surprise Didier greeted us and I immediately recognized him for his stand out service. As someone who served in fine dining for 7 years, I was so impressed by how well he paced our courses, and made us feel like we were the only ones in the restaurant. I believe the mixologist’s name was Alfredo? He was amazing too!\n\nIt was a pleasure to experience food cooked with clear intention (noteworthy compliments to the chef), but Didier absolutely made that night special.\n\nThanks",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
                        "text": "I had the pleasure of going to Equinox 2 years ago as a solo diner, and Didier took care of me. It was such an amazing experience back THEN, that when it was time to decide to hear my birthday dinner was going to be this year, I knew where to go.\n\nTo my surprise Didier greeted us and I immediately recognized him for his stand out service. As someone who served in fine dining for 7 years, I was so impressed by how well he paced our courses, and made us feel like we were the only ones in the restaurant. I believe the mixologist’s name was Alfredo? He was amazing too!\n\nIt was a pleasure to experience food cooked with clear intention (noteworthy compliments to the chef), but Didier absolutely made that night special.\n\nThanks",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "authorAttribution": {
                        "displayName": "Jordan Scott",
                        "uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/116099012205983900760/reviews",
                        "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIN91_HhqwlsooKSC06u2DVMui6eRpAENDXXvB8UoIBB8uWHw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo"
                    },
                    "publishTime": "2024-04-12T19:17:47Z"
