                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "authorAttribution": {
                        "displayName": "Jack Truman",
                        "uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/109589667312663101022/reviews",
                        "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjV671poG7wXeZcXeiN9oCtxmF7voM3_xblpez3kW4QWFSLWUNo=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo"
                    },
                    "publishTime": "2024-08-17T00:08:22Z"
                },
                {
                    "name": "places/ChIJoS6rHx3It4kRIlSnlkEbnaY/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUMxaUxmWXR3RRAB",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "8 months ago",
                    "rating": 2,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "I came up from Alexandria and was so excited to try this place out with the great reviews. It was a huge let down.\n\nThe chicken breading had a good texture but entirely lacked seasoning. The inside of the chicken also had good texture and held up well with the wooden dowel \"bone\" but again, lacked seasoning.\n\nThe greens were just salted, no smoked Paprika, garlic or onion to be tasted at all.\n\nThe Mac n cheese was like macaroni noodles and some sort of either cashew ricotta or a soft tofu, so it didnt give you that mac n cheese vibe. The flavor was almost there but again lacked any pop.\n\nThe cinnamon roll was dense as if they didn't allow the dow to rise or they didn't use enough yeast. Additionally, it was dry and almost hard, I found it difficult to cut with a knife.\n\nI won't be going here again or recommending it, it just doesn't hit the mark. Hip City Veg is the place to go in the D.C. area for vegan food.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
                        "text": "I came up from Alexandria and was so excited to try this place out with the great reviews. It was a huge let down.\n\nThe chicken breading had a good texture but entirely lacked seasoning. The inside of the chicken also had good texture and held up well with the wooden dowel \"bone\" but again, lacked seasoning.\n\nThe greens were just salted, no smoked Paprika, garlic or onion to be tasted at all.\n\nThe Mac n cheese was like macaroni noodles and some sort of either cashew ricotta or a soft tofu, so it didnt give you that mac n cheese vibe. The flavor was almost there but again lacked any pop.\n\nThe cinnamon roll was dense as if they didn't allow the dow to rise or they didn't use enough yeast. Additionally, it was dry and almost hard, I found it difficult to cut with a knife.\n\nI won't be going here again or recommending it, it just doesn't hit the mark. Hip City Veg is the place to go in the D.C. area for vegan food.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
