            "reviews": [
                {
                    "name": "places/ChIJdzAFCdK5t4kRppgHmIpj7Xs/reviews/ChdDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSURyMVpXb3JBRRAB",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a month ago",
                    "rating": 1,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "Went there around 2:15 pm today. The young woman with brown locs gave me an extremely mean look & asked if I was going to order. I stated, in a friendly manner, that I was trying to decide between fries, onion rings, & corn. The two other women beside her said they didn't have fries or corn. I asked for a carrot dog, & was told they didn't have carrots. I stood off to the side while another customer came up & ordered. She was met with smiles, & asked how she was. The man behind her ordered a carrot dog, the woman with locs began processing his order until the customer originally behind me reminded them that they were out of carrots. I will never come here again. I have already mentioned this ordeal to 2 people & intend to tell many more. This is a terrible way to treat paying polite customers. I really hate that I was treated this way, & am honestly trying to understand why it happened.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
