                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "5 months ago",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "5 stars. WONDERFUL food! Defs recomended!\n\nSo, I've only ever gotten through Uber eats, so I can't comment on atmosphere.  As for service, considering I've only ever ordered delivery I haven't had much interaction there, but I can say that if the many times I've ordered here, once they forgot my onion rings and when I called about it, they were friendly and promptly offered me an option for a refund or to pick some up next time I'm in the area (I chose refund and the man encouraged me to call back if I had any more concerns in the future).\n\nBut mostly I wanted to say, the food is friggen fantastic. A bit pricey, as to be expected for healthy, fresh, vegan cuasine, but if you have it, your money will not be waisted here.\nThe first time I ate here, I got the cheese steak and it was so great that I had to check the website twice to make sure it was vegan and that I didn't misunderstand anything. I mean, it was so good and high quality, that I was legitimately worried that I ate meat & cheese and was so relieved and impressed that it was, indeed, vegan!\n\nI now order here every chance I get. I look forward to going to the restaurant in person soon to check it out with my eyeballs & get a feel for atmosphere and more interaction with the staff (which has so far been really good).\n\nFoods I've tried & my opinions:\n•Fantastic onion rings!\n•Delicious sweet potato fries (although more soft then crisp), which go great with the amazingly DELISH hipcityveg sauce (basically a sort of honey mustard).\n•Reg fries are pretty good... like a fresh version of McDonald's (so way better than McD) if that makes any sense.\n•Stk & Chz to die for (this is the item that I thought for sure was not vegan, but was).\n•Crispy chx ranch (I added \"bacon\") is very good, though can kind of tell its not real, but still really great.\n•Ziggy burger was SO yum!\n•Sweet Green Tea is so refreshing with just the right amount of sweet and a hint of another light and fresh flavor that I can't quite put my finger on. I could drink this all day long!\n\nThey have a gluten free bun option, which is really great for those who have more restrictions.\n\nThe brownie and cookie might possibly be my favorite items from here. I always get 2 of each to save for the future and they hold pretty well. I ate all 4 over about a 2 week period and they STILL tasted fresh.\n\nAt one point I tried a swirl shake with nuts and chocolate and it was ok. Not really a repeat for me, but still good. It had a kind of different taste to it that I wasn't really into but not totally against.\n\nAll in all, a wonderful spot for vegans, vegetarians, those with a lot of dietary restrictions, kosher.... or even those with a typical American diet who wants a bang'n dinner (this would be my fiancé, who turns his nose up at my \"weird food\" and yet devours food from hipcityveg)! I have referred this place to many people who all return to me with nothing but great things to say about their experience as well!\n\nI wish every town had a hipcityveg! Unfortunately I live 2 hrs away, but I'll be back as soon as I can be!",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
