                    "rating": 4,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "Great fast casual place. Overall, the food is very good. I built my own bowl with greens, super grains, spicy chicken, and tandoori paneer, plus a bunch of toppings I don't recall. Delicious taste but the texture of the super grains was off...they were very crunchy like they had not been fully cooked. It's possible that was on purpose, but it wasn't my cup of tea.\n\nThe cocktails were pretty tasty and whether you will like them depends on how sweet your taste trends. Loved the cardamom in the mint julep but my husband and I both prefer ours less sweet. The Masala G and T was refreshing and the slight savory touch from the masala spice added some interest.\n\nI also tried the unsweetened spiced tea (recommended) and a few of the other non-alcoholic drinks. They were a bit too sweet for me but would be good blended with the unsweetened tea).\n\nThe chai cookies are tasty; next time I'll bring them home, warm them up, and eat them with tea.\n\nService was quick and friendly. The space is lively and colorful. It can be a bit hard to hear if it's busy because of the high ceilings and reflective surfaces, but that's not a big deal, especially if you're only popping in briefly to eat.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
