                {
                    "name": "places/ChIJ7aCfw2C3t4kRvb6eK8AmDGQ/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUN4MlBTUlpnEAE",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a year ago",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "I had the pleasure of dining at Planta Queen, an Asian-themed vegan venue that has recently opened its doors in DC. With a sister Italian-themed restaurant in Bethesda and plans to open a New Mexican-themed vegan venue soon, Planta Queen is already making waves in the culinary world.\nMy dining experience was nothing short of fantastic. The sushi dishes were undoubtedly the stars of the show, receiving a five-star rating from me. The fact that they were vegan choices that tasted like seafood was truly impressive. The Unagi eggplant nigiri sushi was particularly memorable, with another sushi dish that was torched and had pressed avocado miso truffle glaze that added a delightful flavor to the dish. The Dragon roll was equally as impressive, with its tempura broccoli, spinach, avocado, and spicy unagi sauce. I must also add that the Crispy rice spicy ahi Watermelon avocado sushi plate is not to be missed at Planta Queen. The combination of crispy rice, spicy ahi, and refreshing watermelon and avocado was a delightful surprise that elevated the sushi experience to another level. The flavors and textures were perfectly balanced, making it a memorable and unique dish that I would highly recommend to anyone visiting the restaurant.\nThe crispy gyoza dumplings were another standout dish. The combination of cabbage, carrot, cilantro, mushroom, and chili soy made for a delicious and flavorful bite.\nFinally, the Dan Dan noodles from the wok section of the menu were a definite must-try. The Szechuan kamut, Gavi pan, coconut milk, sesame, and cilantro all combined perfectly to create a dish that was both spicy and satisfying.\nOverall, Planta Queen is a fantastic addition to the DC food scene. The restaurant's commitment to vegan cuisine without sacrificing taste is admirable, and the dishes are expertly crafted with fresh and high-quality ingredients. I am eagerly anticipating the opening of their New Mexican-themed vegan venue and will certainly be returning to Planta Queen in the future.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
                        "text": "I had the pleasure of dining at Planta Queen, an Asian-themed vegan venue that has recently opened its doors in DC. With a sister Italian-themed restaurant in Bethesda and plans to open a New Mexican-themed vegan venue soon, Planta Queen is already making waves in the culinary world.\nMy dining experience was nothing short of fantastic. The sushi dishes were undoubtedly the stars of the show, receiving a five-star rating from me. The fact that they were vegan choices that tasted like seafood was truly impressive. The Unagi eggplant nigiri sushi was particularly memorable, with another sushi dish that was torched and had pressed avocado miso truffle glaze that added a delightful flavor to the dish. The Dragon roll was equally as impressive, with its tempura broccoli, spinach, avocado, and spicy unagi sauce. I must also add that the Crispy rice spicy ahi Watermelon avocado sushi plate is not to be missed at Planta Queen. The combination of crispy rice, spicy ahi, and refreshing watermelon and avocado was a delightful surprise that elevated the sushi experience to another level. The flavors and textures were perfectly balanced, making it a memorable and unique dish that I would highly recommend to anyone visiting the restaurant.\nThe crispy gyoza dumplings were another standout dish. The combination of cabbage, carrot, cilantro, mushroom, and chili soy made for a delicious and flavorful bite.\nFinally, the Dan Dan noodles from the wok section of the menu were a definite must-try. The Szechuan kamut, Gavi pan, coconut milk, sesame, and cilantro all combined perfectly to create a dish that was both spicy and satisfying.\nOverall, Planta Queen is a fantastic addition to the DC food scene. The restaurant's commitment to vegan cuisine without sacrificing taste is admirable, and the dishes are expertly crafted with fresh and high-quality ingredients. I am eagerly anticipating the opening of their New Mexican-themed vegan venue and will certainly be returning to Planta Queen in the future.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
