                {
                    "name": "places/ChIJE3EX2pO3t4kRtfRlVwm6pYg/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUQybzdld0lREAE",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 years ago",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "Cute little café/breakfast and lunch spot perfect for visiting vegans.\n\nMy friend and I stopped by for a lunch after traveling in from NYC.\n\nI ordered the (small) harvest chili which was a huge portion. There were so many veggies, so much protein and nutrients, that I was full from that bowl alone. The flavor was savory and well spiced without being overpowered by tomatoes.\n\nMy friend ordered the (large) southwest salad which she ate 1/2 of because of the huge portion. Also packed with nutrients and flavor.\nShe also ordered a matcha latte which she didn't love, but I did, because it had a predominately oat milk taste.\n\nPlus she ordered the Tuscan kale wrap which neither of us ate then as we were too full. I however, ate it the next day and loved all the textures from the fresh veggies combined with the softness of the wrap.\n\n5 stars because of the customer service; the food tasted good and we enjoyed the atmosphere. However if you are used to eating fried take out/fast food this is not the place for you.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
                        "text": "Cute little café/breakfast and lunch spot perfect for visiting vegans.\n\nMy friend and I stopped by for a lunch after traveling in from NYC.\n\nI ordered the (small) harvest chili which was a huge portion. There were so many veggies, so much protein and nutrients, that I was full from that bowl alone. The flavor was savory and well spiced without being overpowered by tomatoes.\n\nMy friend ordered the (large) southwest salad which she ate 1/2 of because of the huge portion. Also packed with nutrients and flavor.\nShe also ordered a matcha latte which she didn't love, but I did, because it had a predominately oat milk taste.\n\nPlus she ordered the Tuscan kale wrap which neither of us ate then as we were too full. I however, ate it the next day and loved all the textures from the fresh veggies combined with the softness of the wrap.\n\n5 stars because of the customer service; the food tasted good and we enjoyed the atmosphere. However if you are used to eating fried take out/fast food this is not the place for you.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "authorAttribution": {
                        "displayName": "Tamar Gomez",
                        "uri": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100176278212974360487/reviews",
                        "photoUri": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWQJeTu0PznmozOHufiTJRh4TCP8qAUSUoGwP21RD1CKqdQ64D9=s128-c-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba4-br100"
                    },
                    "publishTime": "2022-05-23T19:46:59Z"
                },
                {
                    "name": "places/ChIJE3EX2pO3t4kRtfRlVwm6pYg/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSURHX3Z2Z0JnEAE",
                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 years ago",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "Awesome place and friendly staff. The food is all amazing. I had the spicy salad and it was so full of flavor. I loved the mangoes in it. Definitely will be coming back here regularly. The only thing is I wish their tea list had more details. I got the turmeric ginger and there was a lot of green leaves in it- perhaps green tea but not sure but it would be nice to know the full content or at least if there’s caffeine or not in each tea.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
