                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 months ago",
                    "rating": 4,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "Great vegan spot in the Logan Circle/14th St area. There aren't many good or even decent vegan places, so consider going here and supporting the business if you want to keep having good vegan options in the city.\n\nThe food is the star of the show here, with a pretty good selection of vegan sushi rolls, small dishes, and entrees. The caesar cups are unexpectedly good and satisfying and the queso dip is guaranteed to fill you up. Both are highly recommended.\n\nMains are tough if you have a wheat allergy/GF like me, but the lettuce wraps aren't a bad option, if you don't mind the very salty nature of them.\n\nSubjective take on the sushi is that they're good but I don't care for most of the rolls. They tend to fall apart and having had exceptional vegan sushi at other places in the country, I tend to steer clear of the sushi menu here. For some reason, I've found the vegan sushi at Planta Queen in Coconut Grove/Miami FL to have better execution.\n\nService is better than average. Seats and ambiance are very good, as most vegan places tend to be fast casual. This is definitely a nicer experience and a great place to take friends in town who lean vegan or vegetarian.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
