                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a year ago",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "Really superb modern Indian dining experience. Incredibly creative dishes expertly served.\n\nWe started with the assorted papadam with the trio of chutneys (mango, tomato raisin, and eggplant ginger). Standout was the mango with an honorable mention for the tomato raisin. Papadam was perfectly crisp, and well dried so not oily.\n\nNext was the Masala Crab Cake with mustard seeds, curry leaves, tempered mayo). Creamy and well balanced with a sharp hint of mustard, these were soft and indulgent they could have been eaten with a spoon.\n\nThen it was onto the Truffle Dosa with potatoes and truffle shavings. Soft spicy potatoes nestled inside an elegantly folded dosa, and accompanied with a creamy spread that accented each bite perfectly.\n\nFor our entrees, we had the tandoori lamb chops seasoned with mace, cardamom, cashew nuts, and ginger (succulent and extremely flavorful, very tender) and the chicken Tikka masala (the definite standout, it was smokey and creamy and heaven with each bite).  Highly recommend you get a garlic naan to sop up that savory tikka masala sauce!\n\nFor our veggies, we had the small portions of the bhindi mulagapodi (sauteed okra with onions, lentils, and sesame seeds), baingan achari (eggplant with fennel seeds, fenugreek), and zucchini corn peanut poriyal (curry leaves, lentils, and coconut). All were good, but the eggplant achari was by far the best.\n\nFor dessert, we shared the chocolate samosas with chocolate mint ice cream. It was tremendous, and the delicately crisp samosas paired perfectly with the smokey ice cream.\n\nCocktails were fine, my Sania \r(Bourbon, Spiced Pear-infused Honey, \rAllspice Dram, Lime, Fresh Thyme) was a bit too sweet so I didn't finish it but it was worth a try.\n\nService was excellent, from start to finish.",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
                    "originalText": {
                        "text": "Really superb modern Indian dining experience. Incredibly creative dishes expertly served.\n\nWe started with the assorted papadam with the trio of chutneys (mango, tomato raisin, and eggplant ginger). Standout was the mango with an honorable mention for the tomato raisin. Papadam was perfectly crisp, and well dried so not oily.\n\nNext was the Masala Crab Cake with mustard seeds, curry leaves, tempered mayo). Creamy and well balanced with a sharp hint of mustard, these were soft and indulgent they could have been eaten with a spoon.\n\nThen it was onto the Truffle Dosa with potatoes and truffle shavings. Soft spicy potatoes nestled inside an elegantly folded dosa, and accompanied with a creamy spread that accented each bite perfectly.\n\nFor our entrees, we had the tandoori lamb chops seasoned with mace, cardamom, cashew nuts, and ginger (succulent and extremely flavorful, very tender) and the chicken Tikka masala (the definite standout, it was smokey and creamy and heaven with each bite).  Highly recommend you get a garlic naan to sop up that savory tikka masala sauce!\n\nFor our veggies, we had the small portions of the bhindi mulagapodi (sauteed okra with onions, lentils, and sesame seeds), baingan achari (eggplant with fennel seeds, fenugreek), and zucchini corn peanut poriyal (curry leaves, lentils, and coconut). All were good, but the eggplant achari was by far the best.\n\nFor dessert, we shared the chocolate samosas with chocolate mint ice cream. It was tremendous, and the delicately crisp samosas paired perfectly with the smokey ice cream.\n\nCocktails were fine, my Sania \r(Bourbon, Spiced Pear-infused Honey, \rAllspice Dram, Lime, Fresh Thyme) was a bit too sweet so I didn't finish it but it was worth a try.\n\nService was excellent, from start to finish.",
