                            "relativePublishTimeDescription": "2 years ago",
                            "rating": 5,
                            "text": {
                                "text": "Reading some of the other reviews, I am perplexed.  I'm an Italian woman, and I've yet to eat authentic Italian food in the States, but that doesn't mean I don't love it.  I do!  I wouldn't know authentic Indian food from a pop-tart, but I can tell you that our entire experience was phenomenal (minus waiting for an eternity to use the restroom).  I am very sorry to say that the Indian restaurants near me are filthy.  You have to shut your eyes when eating and turn off your sensibilities, but the food is so good and so complex that we eat it anyway.  Rasika has transformed that thoroughly.  Absolutely upscale, fine-dining experience.  Food was wildly excellent, as was presentation.  You could taste the fresh spices, which is unusual.  Most Indian food I've had is intense in flavor, but not w *fresh* spice as was the case here.  Place was jammed all night long.",
