                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "a year ago",
                    "rating": 5,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "Venturing into the heart of Washington DC, I stumbled upon RASA - a hidden culinary gem that has left me awe-struck and utterly satisfied. From the moment I stepped inside, I was captivated by the inviting ambiance, tasteful decorations, and comfortable seating arrangements.\n\nFinding RASA was a breeze, thanks to its convenient location in downtown DC, and I was delighted to discover an abundance of paid parking options available nearby, making it incredibly hassle-free to access.\n\nThe warm and welcoming staff at RASA added an extra layer of charm to the experience. Greeting me with smiles and genuine enthusiasm, they guided me through their menu, passionately explaining the ingredients and flavors of each dish. Their thoughtful suggestions for pairing items heightened my anticipation and curiosity about what was to come.\n\nNow, let's talk about the food - a symphony of flavors that left my taste buds dancing with delight! I had the pleasure of trying multiple rice bowls, each more enticing than the last. The allo tikki bowl and the roasted vegetables bowl were exceptionally flavorful, with rich gravies and perfectly cooked vegetables. While the spice level was on the milder side, I understood the consideration for diverse palates in the area.\n\nThe naan, a staple in Indian cuisine, was soft, fluffy, and expertly cooked, serving as an ideal accompaniment to the delectable dishes.\n\nIntrigued by the thought of trying a healthier version of samosas, I couldn't resist ordering them. To my delight, they were baked to perfection, boasting a delightful potato filling that left me craving more.\n\nOne aspect that pleasantly surprised me was the affordability of the menu. Compared to many other restaurants nearby, RASA offered an exceptional value for money. The reasonable prices allowed me to explore a variety of dishes without worrying about breaking the bank.\n\nThe seating capacity, accommodating about 20 people inside and a few charming tables outside, created a cozy and intimate setting for a relaxed meal. It's the perfect place to unwind and indulge in the exquisite flavors RASA has to offer.\n\nIn conclusion, RASA surpassed my expectations in every way. The seamless blend of flavors, courteous staff, and inviting ambiance made this dining experience truly unforgettable. As a lover of Indian cuisine, RASA has undoubtedly secured its place as one of my top choices in DC.\n\nWhether you're a seasoned fan of Indian cuisine or simply curious to explore new flavors, I wholeheartedly recommend RASA. From the moment you walk in, you'll be transported on a delightful culinary journey that will leave you yearning for more. With its reasonable prices and exceptional quality, RASA stands tall as a must-visit destination for food enthusiasts looking for an authentic Indian dining experience in downtown DC. I can't wait to return and savor more of the remarkable dishes that this hidden gem has to offer!",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
