                    "relativePublishTimeDescription": "9 months ago",
                    "rating": 3,
                    "text": {
                        "text": "my first time stopping by was exciting! the guy who took my order was patient and friendly. we ordered Nachos which were bursting with flavors and i appreciate that they used kidney beans. the Plant-based Glizzy i got had so much potential but had little to no flavor. the onions, peppers, cheese sauce, lentil chili and even the plant-based hot dog didn’t seem to have no seasoning; no salt nor pepper. btw, i ate the glizzy first\n\nall in all, the shopping center in which it is held is so nice and is expanding in business. they have many businesses owned by kids as well, a health conscious convenient store & smoothie shop, a farmers market, and other food companies\n\nmy real issue is upon arriving and departing this space is that no one really greeted you nor said thank you or goodbye which i think should be important\n\nas someone who has grew up on this side of town, i am SO proud of this space",
                        "languageCode": "en"
                    },
